    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107-a1">

                <pb facs="0200" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg120"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Long to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to request that, if
                    compatible with the views of the Department of State, the thanks of this
                    Department be expressed to the Chilean Government <pb facs="0201" n="121"
                        xml:id="pg121"/> and also to the Chilean navy department for the courtesy
                    and kindness extended to the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Iowa</hi> during
                    her recent docking at Talcahuano, Chile, at the dock yard there under the
                    command of Rear-Admiral Perez. The Department desires particularly to express
                    its appreciation of the courtesy shown to the <hi rendition="#italic">Iowa</hi>
                    and her officers by Rear-Admiral Perez.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Long</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
